(7147364, 1094718, 124190, '<td valign="top">oh hi ! hey....someone actually saw this too...lol my golden retriever Buddy was out on the back forty down by the brook and the crane froze when he saw my dog....oddly enough....my dog didn''t bark or chase him....they just both stared at each other long enough for me to run all the way back inside grab my camera and snap the shot.....guess I owe my dog a bone.....sometimes beauty is best seen straight up....natural...simple.... glad someone appreciated this....it was a HUGE bird and the lighting was perfect with the sun and freshly fallen snow....thanks for your comment.... :-)</td>', 'oh hi ! hey....someone actually saw this too...lol my golden retriever Buddy was out on the back forty down by the brook and the crane froze when he saw my dog....oddly enough....my dog didn''t bark or chase him....they just both stared at each other long enough for me to run all the way back inside grab my camera and snap the shot.....guess I owe my dog a bone.....sometimes beauty is best seen straight up....natural...simple.... glad someone appreciated this....it was a HUGE bird and the lighting was perfect with the sun and freshly fallen snow....thanks for your comment.... :-)', '2013-12-25 21:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7147365, 1094718, 124190, '<td valign="top">oh hi ! hey....someone actually saw this too...lol my golden retriever Buddy was out on the back forty down by the brook and the crane froze when he saw my dog....oddly enough....my dog didn''t bark or chase him....they just both stared at each other long enough for me to run all the way back inside grab my camera and snap the shot.....guess I owe my dog a bone.....sometimes beauty is best seen straight up....natural...simple.... glad someone appreciated this....it was a HUGE bird and the lighting was perfect with the sun and freshly fallen snow....thanks for your comment.... :-)</td>', 'oh hi ! hey....someone actually saw this too...lol my golden retriever Buddy was out on the back forty down by the brook and the crane froze when he saw my dog....oddly enough....my dog didn''t bark or chase him....they just both stared at each other long enough for me to run all the way back inside grab my camera and snap the shot.....guess I owe my dog a bone.....sometimes beauty is best seen straight up....natural...simple.... glad someone appreciated this....it was a HUGE bird and the lighting was perfect with the sun and freshly fallen snow....thanks for your comment.... :-)', '2013-12-25 21:41:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7147450, 1095110, 152094, '<td valign="top">Amazing image and as others have said, taken from a phone, it isn''t the camera gear that takes good pictures its the photographer.<br/> <br/>I''m not sure what airline company this is but they need to pay you some big dollars and use this image in their advertisements.</td>', 'Amazing image and as others have said, taken from a phone, it isn''t the camera gear that takes good pictures its the photographer. I''m not sure what airline company this is but they need to pay you some big dollars and use this image in their advertisements.', '2013-12-26 01:41:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7147602, 1095342, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue: Colors and hues are realistic and seem accurate for the subject displayed. <br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast: The light seems a little be flat to me.  Near the middle of the image, the white edges of the shell appear to be burning out and losing detail.  Other areas you can see the detail of the saw marks quite plainly.  I would like to see it go one way or the other.  As opposed to the current mixture. <br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field: The focus and depth of field are excellent.   <br/> <br/>Personal observations:  With the grain, and the tones, the shell looks almost a little dirty or grubby.  I think I would have liked it better cropped tighter on the top and on the left.  Or maybe even cropped to the edges of the complete (inner) spiral.  Yes I am sitting here cropping the screen with my fingers. :-)  Over all I like the image, and think you definitely earned your 6+ score.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color Saturation and Hue: Colors and hues are realistic and seem accurate for the subject displayed.  Brightness and Contrast: The light seems a little be flat to me.  Near the middle of the image, the white edges of the shell appear to be burning out and losing detail.  Other areas you can see the detail of the saw marks quite plainly.  I would like to see it go one way or the other.  As opposed to the current mixture.  Focus and depth of field: The focus and depth of field are excellent.    Personal observations:  With the grain, and the tones, the shell looks almost a little dirty or grubby.  I think I would have liked it better cropped tighter on the top and on the left.  Or maybe even cropped to the edges of the complete (inner) spiral.  Yes I am sitting here cropping the screen with my fingers. :-)  Over all I like the image, and think you definitely earned your 6+ score.', '2013-12-26 14:17:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148008, 1095289, 119012, '<td valign="top">I like the minimalist approach. The rock anchors the composition nicely. I wish though that its had more pleasing tones and possible a tighter crop as the ground texture tends to fight the rock for attention.</td>', 'I like the minimalist approach. The rock anchors the composition nicely. I wish though that its had more pleasing tones and possible a tighter crop as the ground texture tends to fight the rock for attention.', '2013-12-27 08:27:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148175, 1095327, 14476, '<td valign="top">Fine shot of this colorful bird.  <br/>Low score?  Yeah.<br/>I do wonder what was on the rest of that tree the bird''s clinging to.<br/>It seems just a bit cut off.  More of the branch/trunk might have given better balance to this good shot.<br/>What I''m trying to say, I guess, is that (IMO) the story of this shot is in the bird and tree, rather than the<br/>background you chose to include.</td>', 'Fine shot of this colorful bird.  Low score?  Yeah.I do wonder what was on the rest of that tree the bird''s clinging to.It seems just a bit cut off.  More of the branch/trunk might have given better balance to this good shot.What I''m trying to say, I guess, is that (IMO) the story of this shot is in the bird and tree, rather than thebackground you chose to include.', '2013-12-27 12:32:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148178, 1095327, 116247, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sfalice:</b></div><hr/><i> Fine shot of this colorful bird.  <br/>Low score?  Yeah.<br/>I do wonder what was on the rest of that tree the bird''s clinging to.<br/>It seems just a bit cut off.  More of the branch/trunk might have given better balance to this good shot.<br/>What I''m trying to say, I guess, is that (IMO) the story of this shot is in the bird and tree, rather than the<br/>background you chose to include. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree 100% with your comment. I worried to much about getting its eye in the golden ratio area than the rest of the cropping. I also didn''t capture the full bird in the original photo.</td>', 'Originally posted by sfalice: Fine shot of this colorful bird.  Low score?  Yeah.I do wonder what was on the rest of that tree the bird''s clinging to.It seems just a bit cut off.  More of the branch/trunk might have given better balance to this good shot.What I''m trying to say, I guess, is that (IMO) the story of this shot is in the bird and tree, rather than thebackground you chose to include.   I agree 100% with your comment. I worried to much about getting its eye in the golden ratio area than the rest of the cropping. I also didn''t capture the full bird in the original photo.', '2013-12-27 12:37:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148430, 1095341, 91783, '<td valign="top">This is stunning! beautiful idea and it was executed perfectly. the pop of color is really quite lovely!</td>', 'This is stunning! beautiful idea and it was executed perfectly. the pop of color is really quite lovely!', '2013-12-28 03:38:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7148586, 1095364, 60173, '<td valign="top">I certainly see a "Golden Ratio" here. It''s a decently solid image; it''s sharp, well exposed, etc. I might have preferred a color version, but that''s really a preference thing. There''s nothing "wrong" with the color treatment you chose I don''t think. <br/> <br/>S/he sure is cute. I can almost feel the softness of the fur and the sharpness of the straw. I feel like the newborn has more story to tell that isn''t being told here, and I think the story is what would have given this image a better score. Right now this could be any calf in any barn, anywhere. It''s easily forgettable. You say this was in a petting zoo, so what could be done to tell that story? The challenging part would be making a petting zoo look attractive, which is hard, I know, heh.</td>', 'I certainly see a "Golden Ratio" here. It''s a decently solid image; it''s sharp, well exposed, etc. I might have preferred a color version, but that''s really a preference thing. There''s nothing "wrong" with the color treatment you chose I don''t think.  S/he sure is cute. I can almost feel the softness of the fur and the sharpness of the straw. I feel like the newborn has more story to tell that isn''t being told here, and I think the story is what would have given this image a better score. Right now this could be any calf in any barn, anywhere. It''s easily forgettable. You say this was in a petting zoo, so what could be done to tell that story? The challenging part would be making a petting zoo look attractive, which is hard, I know, heh.', '2013-12-28 15:29:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7149336, 1095330, 20799, '<td valign="top">This is amazing, how did I miss it? Fantastic lighting!</td>', 'This is amazing, how did I miss it? Fantastic lighting!', '2013-12-30 03:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7150760, 1095117, 60173, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your brown, heh. <br/> <br/>The DOF doesn''t seem like enough. My eyes want to focus on the center bit, but it''s not clear enough. It might have been better to stand this fossil up on its edge so all of the surface area would be in your DOF. Maybe this is in a case though and you''re not allowed to do that. In that situation, crack that case open, stand the fossil up, snap its photo, and RUN!!!</td>', 'Congratulations on your brown, heh.  The DOF doesn''t seem like enough. My eyes want to focus on the center bit, but it''s not clear enough. It might have been better to stand this fossil up on its edge so all of the surface area would be in your DOF. Maybe this is in a case though and you''re not allowed to do that. In that situation, crack that case open, stand the fossil up, snap its photo, and RUN!!!', '2014-01-02 13:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7152717, 1095187, 82707, '<td valign="top">Stag, I think you got in touch with your feminine side on this one.... It''s gorgeous!  Grats on TT.</td>', 'Stag, I think you got in touch with your feminine side on this one.... It''s gorgeous!  Grats on TT.', '2014-01-06 04:58:52.000000', NULL, 0);
